                  <provenance type="#e" cert="low"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_434">Oxford, Oxfordshire.
                        St Mary Magdalen College</orgName><p>A 12-volume set from Oseney Abbey,
                        owned by John Green in the fifteenth century, and likely given by him to
                        Magdalen‘They typically, on the verso of the final front flyleaf, have a
                        double inscription in [Green’s] hand; those from MS lat. 121, fol. iv, will
                        serve to illustrate the repeated form: ‘&lt;Constat&gt; M I Grene’
                        (anglicana); ‘Prima pars Biblie cum comuni glosa et habet xj. partes
                        sequentes \in xj. voluminibus/ preter omnium parcium x. li.’(secretary, s.
                        xv med.)’ (Hanna, Magdalen, s.nn.)</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Perhaps John Green (d. by June 1484),
                     headmaster of Winchester, master of the college of S. Michael Royal, London,
                     and master of Whittington College, London</provenance>
